| Topic                          | Syntax / Example                                                                                                 | Explanation                                                                                                                    |
| ------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| **What is a Loop?**            | `for` / `while`                                                                                                  | A loop repeats a block of code multiple times.                                                                                 |
| **Why use Loops?**             | `for i in range(1, 6):`                                                                                          | Loops avoid writing the same code repeatedly.                                                                                  |
| **Types of Loops**             | `for`, `while`                                                                                                   | Python mainly provides `for` and `while` loops.                                                                                |
| **`for` Loop**                 | `for i in range(5):`<br>    `print(i)`                                                                           | Repeats code for each item in an iterable. ([Python documentation][1])                                                         |
| **Basic `for` Syntax**         | `for variable in iterable:`<br>    `code`                                                                        | The variable receives each item from the iterable one by one.                                                                  |
| **`range()`**                  | `range(5)`                                                                                                       | Produces `0, 1, 2, 3, 4`.                                                                                                      |
| **`range(stop)`**              | `range(5)`                                                                                                       | Starts at `0` and stops before `5`.                                                                                            |
| **`range(start, stop)`**       | `range(1, 6)`                                                                                                    | Produces `1, 2, 3, 4, 5`.                                                                                                      |
| **`range(start, stop, step)`** | `range(1, 10, 2)`                                                                                                | Produces `1, 3, 5, 7, 9`.                                                                                                      |
| **Reverse `range()`**          | `range(10, 0, -1)`                                                                                               | Counts backward from `10` to `1`.                                                                                              |
| **Loop through String**        | `for ch in "Python":`                                                                                            | Processes every character in the string.                                                                                       |
| **Loop through List**          | `for x in [10, 20, 30]:`                                                                                         | Processes every item in the list.                                                                                              |
| **Loop through Tuple**         | `for x in (10, 20, 30):`                                                                                         | Processes every item in the tuple.                                                                                             |
| **Loop through Set**           | `for x in {1, 2, 3}:`                                                                                            | Processes each set element.                                                                                                    |
| **Loop through Dictionary**    | `for key in data:`                                                                                               | By default, iterates over dictionary keys.                                                                                     |
| **Dictionary Values**          | `for value in data.values():`                                                                                    | Iterates over dictionary values.                                                                                               |
| **Dictionary Key + Value**     | `for key, value in data.items():`                                                                                | Iterates over both keys and values.                                                                                            |
| **`while` Loop**               | `while condition:`<br>    `code`                                                                                 | Repeats while the condition remains `True`. ([Python documentation][1])                                                        |
| **Basic `while` Example**      | `x = 1`<br>`while x <= 5:`<br>    `print(x)`<br>    `x += 1`                                                     | Prints `1` through `5`.                                                                                                        |
| **Loop Counter**               | `i = 1`<br>`i += 1`                                                                                              | A counter is commonly used with `while` loops.                                                                                 |
| **Infinite Loop**              | `while True:`                                                                                                    | Runs continuously until something stops the loop.                                                                              |
| **Stopping Infinite Loop**     | `while True:`<br>    `if x == 5:`<br>        `break`                                                             | `break` can stop an infinite loop.                                                                                             |
| **`break`**                    | `if x == 5: break`                                                                                               | Immediately terminates the nearest enclosing loop. ([Python documentation][2])                                                 |
| **`continue`**                 | `if x == 5: continue`                                                                                            | Skips the rest of the current iteration and moves to the next iteration. ([Python documentation][2])                           |
| **`pass`**                     | `if x == 5:`<br>    `pass`                                                                                       | Does nothing; useful as a placeholder.                                                                                         |
| **Nested Loop**                | `for i in range(3):`<br>    `for j in range(3):`                                                                 | A loop inside another loop.                                                                                                    |
| **Outer Loop**                 | `for i in range(3):`                                                                                             | The outside loop in a nested-loop structure.                                                                                   |
| **Inner Loop**                 | `for j in range(3):`                                                                                             | The loop inside the outer loop.                                                                                                |
| **Loop `else`**                | `for x in nums:`<br>    `...`<br>`else:`<br>    `...`                                                            | The `else` block runs when the loop completes normally without `break`. ([Python documentation][3])                            |
| **`while-else`**               | `while condition:`<br>    `...`<br>`else:`<br>    `...`                                                          | `else` runs when the `while` condition becomes false, provided the loop wasn't stopped by `break`. ([Python documentation][1]) |
| **`for-else` with Search**     | `for x in nums:`<br>    `if x == 5: break`<br>`else:`<br>    `print("Not found")`                                | Very useful for searching for an item.                                                                                         |
| **Loop with `if`**             | `for i in range(10):`<br>    `if i % 2 == 0:`<br>        `print(i)`                                              | A loop can contain conditions.                                                                                                 |
| **Loop with `if-else`**        | `for i in range(5):`<br>    `if i % 2 == 0:`<br>        `print("Even")`<br>    `else:`<br>        `print("Odd")` | Makes a decision during every iteration.                                                                                       |
| **Loop with `break`**          | `for i in range(10):`<br>    `if i == 5: break`                                                                  | Stops when `i` becomes `5`.                                                                                                    |
| **Loop with `continue`**       | `for i in range(5):`<br>    `if i == 2: continue`<br>    `print(i)`                                              | Skips `2` but continues the loop.                                                                                              |
| **Loop with `pass`**           | `for i in range(5):`<br>    `pass`                                                                               | Loop executes but performs no action.                                                                                          |
| **Accumulator**                | `total = 0`<br>`for x in nums:`<br>    `total += x`                                                              | Used to calculate totals/sums.                                                                                                 |
| **Counter**                    | `count = 0`<br>`for x in nums:`<br>    `count += 1`                                                              | Used to count items or occurrences.                                                                                            |
| **Find Maximum**               | `max_value = nums[0]`                                                                                            | A loop can be used to find the largest value.                                                                                  |
| **Find Minimum**               | `min_value = nums[0]`                                                                                            | A loop can be used to find the smallest value.                                                                                 |
| **Sum of Numbers**             | `total = 0`<br>`for i in range(1, 6):`<br>    `total += i`                                                       | Adds numbers during each iteration.                                                                                            |
| **Multiplication Table**       | `for i in range(1, 11):`<br>    `print(n * i)`                                                                   | A common beginner loop exercise.                                                                                               |
| **Factorial**                  | `fact = 1`<br>`for i in range(1, n+1):`<br>    `fact *= i`                                                       | Calculates `n!`.                                                                                                               |
| **Even Numbers**               | `for i in range(2, 11, 2):`                                                                                      | Prints even numbers from `2` to `10`.                                                                                          |
| **Odd Numbers**                | `for i in range(1, 11, 2):`                                                                                      | Prints odd numbers from `1` to `9`.                                                                                            |
| **Loop through Index**         | `for i in range(len(items)):`                                                                                    | Gives access to list indexes.                                                                                                  |
| **`enumerate()`**              | `for i, value in enumerate(items):`                                                                              | Provides both index and value conveniently.                                                                                    |
| **`zip()` with Loops**         | `for name, age in zip(names, ages):`                                                                             | Iterates through multiple sequences together.                                                                                  |
| **Looping with `input()`**     | `while True:`<br>    `value = input()`                                                                           | Useful for programs that repeatedly ask the user for input.                                                                    |
| **Nested `for` Loop**          | `for i in range(3):`<br>    `for j in range(3):`                                                                 | Often used for patterns, matrices, and tables.                                                                                 |
| **Nested `while` Loop**        | `while i < 3:`<br>    `while j < 3:`                                                                             | A `while` loop can also contain another loop.                                                                                  |
| **Loop Variable**              | `for i in range(5):`                                                                                             | `i` receives the current value on each iteration.                                                                              |
| **Iterable**                   | `[1, 2, 3]`, `"Python"`                                                                                          | An object that can provide its elements one at a time to a loop.                                                               |
| **Iterator**                   | `iter([1, 2, 3])`                                                                                                | An iterator provides elements one at a time using `next()`. ([Python documentation][4])                                        |
| **`iter()`**                   | `it = iter(nums)`                                                                                                | Creates an iterator from an iterable.                                                                                          |
| **`next()`**                   | `next(it)`                                                                                                       | Gets the next item from an iterator.                                                                                           |
| **`StopIteration`**            | `next(it)` after exhaustion                                                                                      | Indicates that an iterator has no more items.                                                                                  |
| **Loop and `return`**          | `def find():`<br>    `for x in nums:`<br>        `return x`                                                      | `return` exits the entire function, not just the loop.                                                                         |
| **Loop Performance**           | `for x in items:`                                                                                                | Direct iteration is generally preferable to manually managing indexes when indexes aren't needed.                              |
| **Loop Control**               | `break`, `continue`                                                                                              | These change the normal execution of a loop.                                                                                   |
| **Loop Termination**           | Condition becomes false / iterable ends / `break`                                                                | A loop eventually needs a termination condition or exhausted iterable.                                                         |


